Viktor 10.10.2026: «В тренере смотри на RANK - подсказка под полем инлайн. И можно ли на завершённом тренинге продолжить по большему количеству эпох?»; «В гайде по LoRA Trainer ты не объяснил все параметры. Я так и не смог полностью сориентироваться по AR WEIGHT и AR ANCHOR, Пересмотри этот гайд, пожалуйста».

· The rank's share of the weights and its size leave the line under its field for the first line of the field's tip (data-tip-head, translated as before).
· The AR knobs' tips say what the trainer does and what was measured on GPU2 (heresy/MISC/claude-trainer-ab): AR weight decides whether the music half learns and how hard its lesson pulls against the anchor (0: the base, a timbre only); the anchor counts as a share of the weight (AdamW sizes every step by its own gradients, so both doubled teach the same: 5 % apart, against 1 % for the same run twice); AR speed is the music half's own throttle (0.5 → 1.0 took it three quarters farther). «How they work ›» beside AR weight opens the guide's new section «The Music Half's Three Knobs».
· «Go on to more epochs…» in a run's ⋯ menu, for a run of the studio's own trainer that has ended with a save: asked how many epochs in all (four more offered), it sends the same run, set and knobs with the steps for them; the lab's run of the same name goes on from the last save and the optimizer's state (lab/trainer/train.py; tried 40 → 60 steps on GPU2). AI-Toolkit's runs and live ones do not offer it.
· Steps' field takes a big set's epochs (its max 20 000 → 1 000 000: 2016 tracks for 12 epochs are 24 192 steps).

Suite: 544/0 in the kitchen.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
